  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/R1l9mcQP8_fFPpXCKLpqMjB_C04lBheQS9R5b4ATj_0.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\nA string of length $L$ is fixed at one end and carries a mass of $M$ at the other end. The mass makes $\\left(\\frac{3}{\\pi}\\right)$ rotations per second about the vertical axis passing through end of the string as shown. The tension in the string is $\\ldots\\ldots$ ML.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "36",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\omega=\\frac{3}{\\pi} \\times 2 \\pi=6 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s} \\\\ & R=L \\sin \\theta\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aboIkjRmqCMUPw36UAN1cH5L8_DBbg3ED2Xy8u0kzpQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nand $T=M \\sqrt{g^2+\\omega^4 R^2}$\nAlso, $T \\sin \\theta=M \\omega^2 \\cdot L \\sin \\theta$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad T=M(36) \\mathrm{L} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad T=36 \\mathrm{ML}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
